I thought this was gonna be kind of short, but it's kind of moderately
lengthed. Enjoy!

Tuesday
Today we had Zone Conference in Yonago! It was a great chance to get a
refresher of some inspiration to keep moving forward in our missionary
work. My English is failing me lol. Today I got a good chance to talk with
Sister Sano. Her favorite food is tomatoes lol, I find that so cute =F0=9F=
=98=82 She
says That after she found out so many people dislike tomatoes she usually
gives a different answer when asked her favorite food. After Zone
Conference, we had interviews with President Sano, which went all right. We
had to really hurry afterwards to make it to the Station on time for our
train! We ended up making it =F0=9F=92=AA Due to some rain, however, it was=
 quite the
slow ride at first, the train fully stopped many times along the way. Saw
some crazy lightning too! When we made it back home, President Hattori and
Brother Hisamune helped us to make it back home with the flat tire. We left
the bikes at the church after they picked them up for us, and we got driven
To the apartment.

Wednesday
Today we went and got the flat tire fixed, and got slightly scolded for not
keeping our tires more pumped. Now I know what kind of tire pressure we
need though, so it should be A-ok. Today we planned on trying some finding
by the university, but it seems like it's still on summer break, so there
weren't really any people around. We ended up going over to the art shop,
and talking with the owner this time. They've done an event or something in
the past with our church, and the owner knew about us a bit. We talked a
lot with Ogawa San, she also gave us some art homework. lol We are gonna
use some of our free time to make some art to bring back to the store
sometime in a week or so. it's gonna get put up somewhere with a bunch of
people=E2=80=99s designs, I'll definitely send a picture if we can make it =
to the
event! After that, we did housing for roughly an hour, with pretty limited
positive responses. But we are doing our best, that's all that the Lord
requires! He will provide those who seek Him in His own time, as long as we
keep working hard! Later today we had kids Eikaiwa, followed up by adult
Eikaiwa. It was back to back craziness, but it was really awesome.

Thursday
Today was SKK, so we mostly just planned. However, we did get to have a
phone call with Brother Katayama, and Sister Ushio suddenly dropped by the
church with some food for us, as well as some bookmarks she made. She is
the sweetest! Last Sunday she also gave us each a cute little hand towel.
So generous, and such a great example.

Friday
Today we went back to the university, entered without permission and
surprised the front office again. This time I had my camera around my neck
too and everyone was sooooo sussed out lol. The same nice teacher from
before talked with us though, and Said I'm not suspicious because it's my
second time. We inquired as to if we could participate in the campus clubs
even if we aren't students, and uh, well, we can't lol. But! He told us
again if we can find a student friend that we kind of have a window into
things. He was nice enough to also tell us when summer break ends, which is
in like 2 weeks. He suggested that if we're looking for young people to
meet with that we should work at a nearby Combini lol. Super nice
suggestion, probably not gonna work out but we love the effort and ideas on
his part haha. After that, we did some more housing nearby, also to not
exactly much avail. We're gonna keep pressing forward though. We did have a
few nice people we met, and technically one guy said if he had interest
he'd pull up to our church/eikaiwa. He kept saying =E2=80=9CIF I'm interest=
ed, IF
I'm interested=E2=80=9D lol. Tonight we had Game night back at the church, =
and it
was an arousing success! (I know this is the wrong word Mom, but it was
just too funny not to use =F0=9F=98=82=F0=9F=98=82 please erase it before y=
ou send out the
email =F0=9F=98=80 =F0=9F=98=82) Today one of Nishioka San=E2=80=99s friend=
s came!!! Nishioka san
invited her and even drove to the church with her the day before to show
her what it's like. HOW IS NISHIOKA SAN NOT A MEMBER. Lol. Anyways, her
friends name is Taguchi san. She is like super super way too humble lol.
She ended up having a great time, and she even brought donuts!! We shared a
spiritual thought at the endaiI think she also liked it. Nishioka san also
convinced Taguchi san and her Husband?! to join us for family home evening
on Monday night. What a huge blessing! I pray that they will both be
touched by the spirit, and continue to develop a relationship with the
members here. I also got to play some ping pong with Matsuoka San, and she
told me she is getting the art I made for her framed lol. She Wants my
business card to go with it. I hope that she can tell how much we care
about her and that she will continue to seek out our message of the Gospel.

Saturday
Today we had a pretty cool experience. We were able to visit Sister Magi
and her roommates to give Sister Magi a priesthood blessing. Her two
roommates she was with are both from the Philippines, and were both so
grateful for us to come and bless Sister Magi. She's been feeling sick this
last week, and hasn't been able to make it to work. President Hattori drove
us, and Brother Koumoto also came with us. We brought them a treat to
share, and it was a really neat experience. Kind of relieving to talk with
super open and friendly people lol. I love Filipinos =F0=9F=94=A5 What's ev=
en cooler,
is Sister Magi invited them both to come to church! We also asked them to
come, and they both said sure! Huge miracle!! After driving back to the
church, (and eating some Taiyaki on the way back) we studied from the Book
of Mormon with Brother Koumoto and President Hattori. Pretty awesome day.

Sunday
In the end, only one of Sister Magi=E2=80=99s friends was able to make it. =
Her name
is Jamcy. I sat in between the two of them and interpreted the Sacrament
meeting the best I could. Today was kind of a big day for Jamcy. She kind
of distanced herself from religion for the past year or two due to the way
her church responded to some issue or event back in the Philippines. I
think mostly from the awesome example Sister Magi is setting, she's had the
desire to build back up her relationship with God. Today during second hour
I was also able to introduce her to The Book of Mormon, and she was
immediately intrigued. I gave her a copy, and she's going to start reading
it. I explained to her how it connects to the Bible somewhat, but hopefully
the spirit did some of the explaining, I don't feel like I did a great job.
I felt the spirit all of today though. It was a super cool chance to get to
know Jamcy (27 btw) and introduce her to our church! She said she was so
relieved to have people to speak with in English, and I think she also felt
the spirit. What an amazing Sacrament meeting! I'm so grateful. After
church, we visited the Yamauchi family with President Hattori, as well as
brother Ikegami. It was a good chance to show our support for less active
members, and I pray that they will both feel the desire and need to come
more fully back into the arms of the Savior.

It's been a really really really hard week for me emotionally due to some
stuff I shouldn't really go into much detail about. But look at all of
these great experiences and miracles even through the hard times. I'm so so
grateful for God's hand in my life. As long as I am pressing forward with
the desire to do good, and love those around me, I know I will make it
through whatever comes my way. I am grateful for your prayers, and I am
grateful for you.

Yes, you! I love you so so so much! Each and every one of you are so
precious to me. Please keep your head up, and know that there are others
going through trials too! Also know that God understands your trials better
than you do! Be humble. And choose the hard right over the easy wrong.

Guess what, it's gonna be hard! but it's 1000000% worth it, thanks to the
Savior, Jesus Christ.

Love you guys!

--000000000000376071063e37597c
